[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6055987457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124269#issuecomment-6055987457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124269","id":6055987457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaPcJAQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:33:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:33:44Z","body":"This is pretty verbose, did you use AI to write it? Please see [this](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#for-contributors)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6055987457/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6076586873","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124269#issuecomment-6076586873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124269","id":6076586873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABajFbeQ","user":{"login":"Adolar13","id":18741460,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzQxNDYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18741460?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13","html_url":"https://github.com/Adolar13","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adolar13/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T07:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T07:36:32Z","body":"Thanks for the quick answer and you are right on both. I asked my agent to look through github if the issue is already reported and draft a text if not. He went out of his way und directly posted it. I've withdrawn its permission to do so, so this does not happen again in the future. Here is a minimal issue written in my own words:\n\n### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nMeta Quest 3S / Vulkan / Mobile renderer / OpenXR\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith `rendering/viewport/hdr_2d` enabled, the image in the headset is much darker than with it disabled. My agent said the possible cause is, that the tonemapper skips the sRGB conversion when HDR 2D is enabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create an OpenXR project with the Mobile renderer, with a WorldEnvironment and a lit mesh.\n2. Run it on a Quest 3 or 3s with `rendering/viewport/hdr_2d` disabled.\n3. Enable `rendering/viewport/hdr_2d` and run again: the whole image is much darker.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A\n\nIf you want me to remove or ammend the verbose text, I can do so. Sorry again. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6076586873/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6086801472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124269#issuecomment-6086801472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124269","id":6086801472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABas04QA","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T18:23:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T18:23:55Z","body":"> My agent said the possible cause is, that the tonemapper skips the sRGB conversion when HDR 2D is enabled.\n\nWhen HDR 2D is enabled, the sRGB conversion happens in blit.glsl for the Mobile renderer. When HDR 2D is disabled, the sRGB conversion happens in tonemap.glsl. This is a very low likelyhood for the cause of the bug, but not entirely impossible.\n\nA more likely possibility is that the luminance multiplier is being incorrectly applied in your scenario. I presume you can't reproduce this issue when not targeting XR?\n\nIn short, when HDR 2D is disabled the values are scaled by `0.5` when saving it to a non-floating point buffer to be able to record a higher dynamic range than would normally be possible. These values then need to be scaled by `2.0` later to undo this temporary scaling.\n\nSo it's possible that the HDR 2D mode is incorrectly applying the `0.5` scaling (and correctly not scaling it back by `2.0` later). Just a wild guess, mind you.\n\nIt would be good to know exactly which version of the engine introduced this bug so we can track down the PR that caused it. You can use the builds in the [download archive](https://godotengine.org/download/archive/) to determine this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6086801472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6204374064","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124269#issuecomment-6204374064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124269","id":6204374064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcc88MA","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T23:24:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T23:24:54Z","body":"> 5\\. When HDR 2D is enabled, the sRGB conversion happens in blit.glsl for the Mobile renderer. When HDR 2D is disabled, the sRGB conversion happens in tonemap.glsl. This is a very low likelyhood for the cause of the bug, but not entirely impossible.\n\nThis actually is the cause, with XR we do not go beyond the tonemapper as the tonemapper outputs to the buffers supplied by OpenXR.\n\nThese buffers also aren't setup for HDR so this is not functional (at the moment).\n\nThe only exception is Apple Vision Pro which does have full HDR output support.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6204374064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6220567535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124269#issuecomment-6220567535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124269","id":6220567535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcsZT7w","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-16T17:01:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T17:01:11Z","body":"Ah, neat. I guess all the suff in `APPLY_LENS_DISTORTION` of `blit.glsl` is for Apple Vision Pro only(?)\n\nThis would mean debanding is also broken for XR when HDR2D is enabled on both Mobile and Forward+. (Ever since my improvements were merged in 4.5 or 4.6, I can't remember which.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6220567535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]